  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1032 PM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nLatest medium and long term ensembles continue to suggest that our\nhigh pressure will start shifting west slightly Monday into\nWednesday. This will allow shortwave disturbances to cross into\nthe area on northwest flow aloft, and provide more chances for\nevening and overnight storms, especially Tuesday and Wednesday.\nTemperatures also may drop at least for a day or two next week\npartially due to the increased cloud cover, but also just in\nresponse to height falls and being remove from the high pressure\ncenter. Unfortunately, it looks like the high does try to squeeze\nback to the east late week into next weekend, so chances are we\nwill see at least a few more days of widespread 100-105 degree\nheat to finish off August. Hopefully early September will see the\ndemise of our high pressure, as some longer range ensemble \nmembers are suggesting. \n\nWard",
